## SEVERITY / VERDICT
*Blocker:* a path beyond the 8; any product, support, workflow, package or lockfile change; a removed line beyond the 4 accounted; an existing assertion LOOSENED (an old name red at base now green at head under any mutant, or a table that lost a row, or a `BOOT_LLM_PROVIDER` / `KEY` change that stops the old protection); a lost test name; a failed full verify or a count that is not 5005/305 equal to the committed file; a count mismatch the verify does not catch (Check 4c control fails); a cell RED on main or at head (a product defect: report it, fix nothing); **a named target mutant SURVIVING at head** (any of: MadminArray, MadminIncl, the RD-860 title mutant, M10, M14b, M865a, M865b, M863-k, M871a-d, M857-f, MB_S_STARTUP, MB_S_RESTORE, MB_S_INIT; with the single exception the `customer` cell, which is graded per Check 3); a NEW CodeQL alert with security severity high+ or rule severity `error` on the PR ref; a gitleaks finding; a person name, card id or secret in an added line or message; an audit failure that main's own tree does NOT reproduce; the head moved. *Major:* a builder claim contradicted (34 cells; 5005/305; 0 lost / 34 added; the per-mutant red counts); a new cell no mutant turns red and not a declared control (beyond `customer`); the RD-866 2x2 not as claimed; `AI_RATE_LIMIT_MAX` or the plant changing an old cell's behaviour; a mutant killed by fewer cells than claimed; a CodeQL alert that is NEW but below both thresholds. *Minor/Note:* the `d5c516f` message overstating M871a by one; the unsupported `customer` reason in the builder STATUS; the `_updated` line in the counts diff; the builder's pre-existing `existsSync` notes; node version differing from CI; load-rule remarks; the shared counts path with #67 (PRE-CLEARED, a NOTE).
**VERDICT RULES.** GO needs every check-run at the head completed and green, both CodeQL thresholds met on a complete scan (all three analyses listed), 0 findings above Note. **While `audit-production-deps` is red the verdict is at most GO WITH FINDINGS and its line ends ` (CI red: audit-production-deps; base fact of main's own tree, not this lane)` when Check 5b proves the base cause, else NO GO.** While `build` or the JavaScript analysis is pending the line adds ` (CI pending: <names>)`. A NO GO sends a fix round to a new builder seat on this branch: state the fix-shape in prose and a ONE-line question for the product owner only if a ruling is needed. Round 1 of 2; a second NO GO on the same class of finding goes to the product owner. **Escalation (binding): a Sonnet G2 that finds a security-shaped issue hands the PR to tier 1:** STOP (`STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <the change and why>`) if the delta holds a path beyond the 8, any file under `backend/`, `static/`, `.github/` or `scripts/` other than the counts file, a package or lockfile change, a raw non-ASCII byte in an added line, a new dependency, a request that leaves loopback (other than GitHub GETs and the npm registry as `npm ci` itself reaches it), a secret, or a security-shaped finding you cannot classify by the list above (your own scratch mutants are scratch tamper, not a delta).
**First line of STATUS (the verdict line; at Step 0 the placeholder `GATE VERDICT B592: PENDING`):** `GATE VERDICT B592: pr106 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> @ 303fb29 (round 1 of 2 - delta <8 paths, 9 commits, +254 -4; product files 0 y/n; removed lines 4 y/n; non-ASCII added 0 y/n> - loosening <n of 4 changed lines loosened; env-changed existing cells n; kill-set monotonic y/n> - names <lost n, added n of 34; duplicates 0 y/n> - cells <34 new; red under a named mutant n plus declared controls n; targets killed n of m; survivors <names|none>; OLD-side survivors reproduced n of m; controls c0 c1 c2 c3 cw-weak as expected y/n; own mutants n; customer cell: <killed by X|killed by none>> - counts <5005/305 equal to the file y/n; keys changed {_updated,tests} y/n; stub control 5004 and 5006 fired y/n|VOID> - verify head <PASS 5005/305|state> - audit <red at head y/n; red at main's tree y/n; advisory GHSA-27r3-jxmh-p828> - CI <n completed success of n; pending <names|none>; failing <names|none>> - CodeQL <analyses n of 3 at the head; open alerts n; new high+ n; new error n> - merge <ahead 9 behind 0 y/n; main sha7 at start and end> - gitleaks rc <n>)`. Then the sections: Step 0 (sha256s, slot count), REFUSE counts, PINS (start and verdict), instrument and load, Checks 1-8 each with the FAIL clock and the evidence path, findings `B592-n` (severity, `path:line` at the head, instrument, FAIL met, fix-shape in prose, evidence class MEASURED AT RUNTIME / PROBED / READ ONLY; "none" is valid), the removed-lines old-versus-new table, the mutant tables (mutant, file, tree, anchor count, sha256 before/after, ran, red cells by name, restore proof) and the cells kill table (34 rows), FOR TUESDAY (the verdict in plain words; what stands between the PR and a green landing, naming the audit red and the pending checks; the `customer` cell; the commit-message note; the counts order against #67), FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections / processes, ports and trees left, **U